  <h2>2. Project Abstract</h2>
  <p>Overview of the project, the problem solved, and the unique approach.</p>

  <table>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Project Name</td>
      <td class="value">Sivan</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">One liner description (one sentence, limit to 200 chars)</td>
      <td class="value">Sivan AI is a WhatsApp-native AI payment assistant that locks service agreements, handles fee splits, and bridges USDC to local bank payouts for emerging market freelancers and traders.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">What problem are you solving and why is it important?</td>
      <td class="value">
        Emerging markets face a severe trust deficit in social commerce and freelance transactions, resulting in high rates of payment defaults and cart abandonment. Digital creative freelancers and small agencies coordinate work through scattered chat logs, leading to misaligned terms and disputes. Traditional Cash-on-Delivery (CoD) is highly inefficient—up to 30% of physical orders are rejected at the door, forcing sellers to absorb double shipping costs. 
        Additionally, local freelancers face excessive transaction delays, high intermediary fees, and complex Web3 onboarding requirements when trying to receive international stablecoin payments.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">What is your solution to that problem?</td>
      <td class="value">
        Sivan provides a WhatsApp-based project and service coordination software platform. It allows users to document service agreements, organize project terms, and manage client communications directly inside familiar chat screens. Sivan helps users coordinate protected transaction workflows through licensed payment partners. 
        Buyers fund agreements using local fiat or USDC, and Sivan manages transaction records, verification of delivery proof, and automated local currency payouts straight to the seller's bank account, abstracting all blockchain complexity from the end user.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Why hasn't this problem been solved yet? What are the barriers?</td>
      <td class="value">
        The barriers were technical, operational, and UX-related:
        <ul class="bullet-list">
          <li><strong>UX Friction:</strong> Conversational interfaces previously relied on error-prone open-text parsing. Sivan AI now uses native Twilio Content API templates with interactive WhatsApp quick-reply buttons, reducing all input syntax errors to 0%.</li>
          <li><strong>Fee Model Ambiguity:</strong> No existing tool asked users who should bear transaction fees. Sivan AI now intelligently asks each party — Buyer pays, Seller pays, or Split 50/50 — and applies it automatically to the agreement and payout calculation.</li>
          <li><strong>Onboarding Complexity:</strong> Traditional Web3 onboarding requires users to manage private keys, gas tokens, and swap protocols. Sivan AI abstracts this entirely through developer-controlled programmable wallets.</li>
          <li><strong>Regulatory and Banking Gaps:</strong> Connecting stablecoins directly to local bank payouts was historically complex. Sivan AI solves this by routing payments through licensed regional infrastructure partners (Flutterwave, Monnify, Nomba) who perform regulated money movement with name-matched account verification.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Why are you and your team uniquely suited to solve this?</td>
      <td class="value">
        Our team has hands-on experience building production-grade fintech AI systems, secure ledger architectures, and conversational AI agents. We have successfully designed and deployed:
        <ul class="bullet-list">
          <li>A double-entry accounting ledger with automatic trust-tier enforcement and exposure limits.</li>
          <li>Native Twilio Content API interactive button templates for a fully guided, zero-error WhatsApp UX — including a live fee payer selection step (Buyer / Seller / Split).</li>
          <li>Multi-provider banking fallbacks with account name verification scoring (Nomba, PalmPay, Monnify, Flutterwave).</li>
          <li>Cloudflare R2-based evidence storage for delivery proof validation.</li>
          <li>63 passing automated tests across end-to-end, rate limit, and conversational flow scenarios.</li>
        </ul>
        We operate directly within the target market (Lagos, Nigeria) and have a deep, lived understanding of social commerce trust deficits.
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h2>3. Product Alignment Track</h2>
  <p>Current product status, integration details, and planned usage of Circle stablecoins.</p>

  <table>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Is your project currently live in production?</td>
      <td class="value">Yes, Sivan's local fiat (Naira) service agreement workflow is live in production. The USDC autonomous settlement bridge is currently running on Solana devnet/testnet.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Are you live on Arc?</td>
      <td class="value">No, but we plan to integrate Circle's Arc/Developer platform to power automated on-chain compliance and user identity credentials as we scale.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Which other chain(s) are you currently live on?</td>
      <td class="value">Solana (Devnet/Testnet for USDC autonomous releases). We plan to expand to Polygon for EVM compatibility.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Which Circle products are currently integrated into your project?</td>
      <td class="value">
        <ul class="bullet-list">
          <li><strong>USDC:</strong> Integrated as the base stablecoin asset for P2P service agreements, providing a stable store of value.</li>
          <li><strong>Programmable Wallets (Sandbox):</strong> Used to host developer-controlled wallets for agreement deposits, abstracting private keys for web2 users.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Which Circle products do you plan to integrate into your project?</td>
      <td class="value">
        <ul class="bullet-list">
          <li><strong>Circle Programmable Wallets (Production Upgrade):</strong> To deploy user-controlled smart contract wallets natively for every registered WhatsApp user, securing their USDC deposits.</li>
          <li><strong>Circle CCTP (Cross-Chain Transfer Protocol):</strong> To enable seamless, low-cost cross-chain transfers of USDC directly through simple chat interactions.</li>
          <li><strong>Circle Gas Station / Fee Sponsorship:</strong> To abstract transaction gas fees, allowing buyers to fund service agreements with USDC without needing native blockchain gas tokens.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h2>4. Milestones and Timelines</h2>
  
  <table>
    <tr>
      <th>Milestone</th>
      <th>Details & Description</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Milestone 01: Circle Programmable Wallets Integration (Months 1-2)</td>
      <td>
        Integrate Circle's Programmable Wallets API into the core service backend. This will automatically provision a secure, gas-sponsored wallet for every user who registers their WhatsApp number, eliminating seed phrase management.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Milestone 02: Multi-Chain USDC Agreement & CCTP Routing (Months 3-4)</td>
      <td>
        Deploy non-custodial smart contracts on Solana and Polygon. Implement Circle CCTP to allow buyers on other EVM chains to deposit USDC which bridges natively to the seller's preferred chain.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Milestone 03: Circle Mint & Automated Bank Payout Off-Ramp (Months 5-6)</td>
      <td>
        Connect Circle Mint APIs and local fiat partner rails (via Sivan's Multicurrency Engine) to enable automatic, low-cost off-ramps from USDC straight to local Nigerian bank accounts upon buyer release.
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h2>5. Project Traction and Roadmap</h2>

  <table>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Current Traction</td>
      <td class="value">
        Sivan AI is live in closed beta for Naira-denominated service agreements. Recent milestones achieved:
        <ul class="bullet-list">
          <li><strong>Native Interactive Templates:</strong> Registered 7 native Twilio Content API button templates (Welcome, Help &amp; Guide, Deal Actions, Confirmation, Fee Payer Selector, Seller Invite, Delivery), reducing all input syntax errors to 0%.</li>
          <li><strong>Fee Model Selector:</strong> Sivan AI now intelligently prompts users to select who pays the service agreement fee — Buyer, Seller, or Split 50/50 — and forwards this selection to the Core API automatically.</li>
          <li><strong>Production Test Suite:</strong> 63 automated tests across end-to-end flows, rate limit scenarios, conversational wizard steps, and async Twilio webhook handling — all passing green.</li>
          <li><strong>Multi-Provider Fallbacks:</strong> Live payment failover across Flutterwave → Monnify → Nomba with name-matching score verification.</li>
          <li><strong>500+ waitlist signups</strong> at sivantech.online with a production landing page and linked pitch deck.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Public Analytics Dashboard Link</td>
      <td class="value">N/A - Sivan's volume and transaction metrics are kept confidential and restricted to the authenticated operations management console for platform security and client privacy compliance.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Are you funded?</td>
      <td class="value">No, we are currently bootstrapped and self-funded.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">Technical Roadmap Overview</td>
      <td class="value">
        Our roadmap is divided into three key development phases:
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Phase 1 (✅ Live &amp; Complete):</strong> Sivan AI conversational wizard with native Twilio interactive buttons, fee payer selection (Buyer / Seller / Split), double-entry ledger bookkeeping, Cloudflare R2 evidence sync, multi-provider fiat (Naira) payment integration, Telegram admin dashboard, and a full 63-test automated test suite.</li>
          <li><strong>Phase 2 (Immediate — Grant Funded):</strong> Circle Programmable Wallets API integration for gas-less, non-custodial on-chain USDC storage. Each WhatsApp-registered user automatically receives a managed smart contract wallet.</li>
          <li><strong>Phase 3 (Scale):</strong> Multi-chain USDC routing via Circle CCTP, Circle Gas Station sponsorship for the first 10,000 users, and automated stablecoin-to-local-bank payout bridges on Solana and Polygon.</li>
        </ol>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="label">How will this grant support your technical roadmap?</td>
      <td class="value">
        The grant funding will be utilized to achieve our roadmap goals:
        <ul class="bullet-list">
          <li><strong>Infrastructure Costs:</strong> Funding Twilio interactive template fees, R2 storage nodes, and PostgreSQL cluster hosting.</li>
          <li><strong>Security Audits:</strong> Conducting a third-party smart contract audit of the USDC agreement wrappers.</li>
          <li><strong>Gas Sponsorship:</strong> Subsidizing initial on-chain gas costs (via Circle's Gas Station) for the first 10,000 users.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>

